{"availability":"available","full":"larszu/lz-media-station","name":"lz-media-station","description":"Sensor-triggered media station: plays video when someone approaches (HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor or camera detection), with web admin, display mode and multi-station manager. Raspberry Pi, macOS, Windows.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2025-08-27T10:36:20Z","updated":"2026-10-07T22:12:33Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://larszu.github.io/lz-media-station/","topics":["computer-vision","digital-signage","hc-sr04","interactive-installation","iot","kiosk","media-player","motion-detection","presence-detection","python","raspberry-pi","ultrasonic-sensor","video-player"],"demo":"https://larszu.github.io/lz-media-station/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T02:09:27.256Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T02:09:27.256Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T02:09:27.256Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T02:09:27.256Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Digital signage that reacts to people. Layouts with regions, a weekly programme, widgets and instant messages — driven by a distance sensor, a button, a webhook or the clock. Runs on a Raspberry Pi and on any Mac/Windows computer, fully offline, with a desktop manager for many stations.","The established systems are good at playing content on a schedule. Where users most often complain — per-screen fees, cloud lock-in, clumsy layout and schedule editors, no real preview, slow publishing — this station takes a different route:","What it deliberately does not do (yet): frame-accurate video walls, automatic transcoding, PDF/PowerPoint import — see the issues."],"features":["Layouts with regions: a layout divides the screen into percent","Layout editor with live preview: draw regions on a canvas (drag,","resize at the corners, 5 % grid — mouse and one finger on a phone), build play